  "sourceCommitScope": "Benchmark implementation snapshot for SB7.2 (scorer sb-7.2): SB7.1's Meridian product, SB7 contract, starter (sb7.1/starter), fixtures and vendor with a 3D-weighted scorer (score_sb72.py wraps score_sb71.py), the framed default camera and overview legibility (product_probe_sb72.mjs = product_probe_sb71.mjs under the SB7.2 profile), public excellence rungs and a 180 ms stream-apply rung (sb72-thresholds.json), and run_build.py --sb72 through isolated_tiers.py. Release metadata and the validation receipt are added by the manifest commit. Call budget and wallet guard (5ae66cd5e, owner-approved 2026-10-02): run_build.py passes --max-turns bench_budget.CALL_BUDGET (150) to every isolated single-model entrant's goose run (swarm entrants unbudgeted), records budget{max_calls, calls_used, stopped_by} in agent, verdict and model-cost.json, scores a call-budget or wallet-guard stop instead of refusing it, and with BENCH_MAX_USD set SIGTERMs an OpenRouter entrant's pid once its billed generations reach the limit; bench_budget.py and test_bench_budget.py are new, bench_cost.py and bench_rescore.py changed with it; scorer bytes unchanged. SB7.2 public contract trim (2026-10-02, f202fcaab): isolated_tiers.py gains a per-tier `public` table that run_build.py renders into the workdir; SB7.1 still renders spec-build-sb7.md and sb7.1/VISUAL-CONTRACT.md (receipt contract tuple unchanged, test-pinned); SB7.2 renders its own sb7.2/SB7-CONTRACT.md, sb7.2/VISUAL-CONTRACT.md and sb7.2/STARTER.md (72,107 -> 35,848 bytes; three refuter-found measured requirements restored: newest-first notifications, /api/events seq > after ascending, /api/drafts?state= filter) and its prompt gains a definition of done and the 150-call budget; score_sb72.py hashes the SB7.2 contract files; release_manifest.py pins the two new files. Scoring bytes (probes, thresholds, check logic) unchanged. Harness refreeze 2026-10-10 for the app that also bundles Forge 2.0: bench_budget.py, isolated_tiers.py, run_build.py, release_manifest.py and test_bench_budget.py moved for the FORGE20 tier only (call budget 300 on that tier; this tier stays at 150) - scorer, probe, spec, fixtures and thresholds bytes unchanged; run_build.invoke() proven byte-identical for this tier on both sides.",
